TREE | $ | record | id,forms
TREE | $/id | text | role
TREE | $/forms | record | Subj,Obj,In,With,To,About,Of
TREE | $/forms/Subj | text | <empty>
TREE | $/forms/Obj | text | <empty>
TREE | $/forms/In | text | in
TREE | $/forms/With | text | with
TREE | $/forms/To | text | to
TREE | $/forms/About | text | about
TREE | $/forms/Of | text | of
# Each LOOKUP calls real TableMorphology.form("prep:role", {FeatureKey("Case"): FeatureValue(case)}), preserving source order.
LOOKUP | 01 | prep:role | Case=Subj | <empty>
LOOKUP | 02 | prep:role | Case=Obj | <empty>
LOOKUP | 03 | prep:role | Case=In | in
LOOKUP | 04 | prep:role | Case=With | with
LOOKUP | 05 | prep:role | Case=To | to
LOOKUP | 06 | prep:role | Case=About | about
LOOKUP | 07 | prep:role | Case=Of | of
# Missing form, missing lexeme, wrong-case lexeme and wrong-case feature value must throw, not return empty text.
LOOKUP_ERROR | prep:role | Case=MissingCase | no form
LOOKUP_ERROR | prep:missing | Case=In | no form
LOOKUP_ERROR | prep:Role | Case=In | no form
LOOKUP_ERROR | prep:role | Case=in | no form
LOOKUP_ERROR | prep:role | <empty-bundle> | no form
# Tiny test-owned ConstructionTemplate: one SlotTemplate(name="prep", category="prep", requiredFeatures=["Case"]), separator=" "; LexemeFeatures returns emptyMap(); lexicalSlots={"prep":"role"}.
# RealizedSentence uses Kotlin IntRange semantics: `0 until 2` = 0..1; `0 until 0` is an empty range, yet the slot key is present.
REALIZER | fixture.preposition | Case=In | text=in | slot=prep | span=0 until 2
REALIZER | fixture.preposition | Case=Obj | text=<empty> | slot=prep | span=0 until 0
REALIZER_ERROR | fixture.preposition | Case=In | missing lexical slot prep | throws
# Obj's empty lookup is not the production recipe's optional-slot omission; the latter needs a separate full-course parity check.
# Negative authored sources are complete UTF-8 LF files. Each has one fault: unknown keys are additions to all seven valid Case keys, never replacements. Coordinates identify the first required diagnostic token; omitted keys point to the containing forms record's opening brace.
